; mod_min_by_minus_one: i64::MIN % -1 is mathematically 0, which is
; representable, so it yields 0 rather than raising.
;
; The paired division i64::MIN / -1 does overflow -- its quotient 2^63 has
; no i64 -- so DIV and MOD part company on exactly this operand pair.
; See div_min_by_minus_one.

PUSH -9223372036854775808
PUSH -1
MOD
HALT
